{
  "_comment": [
    "Signature database for rc-carve (SPEC.md section 5.5).",
    "",
    "A data file rather than a hardcoded table so it can be extended without",
    "recompiling. Starts at ~40 high-value formats and grows toward 350+.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  id          stable identifier, also the validator key",
    "  ext         file extension to emit",
    "  category    image | video | audio | document | archive | database | other",
    "  header      hex bytes at the start of the file",
    "  header_mask optional hex mask; a zero nibble means 'ignore this nibble'",
    "  header_off  byte offset of the header within the file (default 0)",
    "  footer      optional hex bytes that terminate the file",
    "  max_size    hard ceiling in bytes",
    "  validator   optional validator id; 'none' means header match only",
    "",
    "max_size is mandatory and matters more than it looks. A format with no",
    "footer is terminated only by this number, so a single spurious header",
    "would otherwise swallow gigabytes of unrelated disk and produce one",
    "enormous bogus candidate. Values are set generously above realistic file",
    "sizes but far below 'the rest of the volume'.",
    "",
    "Ordering note: entries whose header is a prefix of another must appear",
    "after the more specific one. ZIP is the important case - every OOXML file",
    "and every JAR is a ZIP, so the ZIP entry sniffs its content to decide what",
    "it really is rather than emitting .zip for all of them."
  ],
